#: ../../source/references_paper-explainer.md:249
msgid "Common mistakes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_paper-explainer.md:251
msgid ""
"**Trying to cover the whole paper.** A 5-minute video can explain ONE "
"core insight well. Covering everything means explaining nothing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_paper-explainer.md:252
msgid ""
"**Reading the abstract as narration.** Academic writing is designed for "
"readers, not listeners. Rewrite in conversational language."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_paper-explainer.md:253
msgid ""
"**Showing notation without meaning.** Never show a symbol without first "
"showing what it represents visually."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_paper-explainer.md:254
msgid ""
"**Skipping the motivation.** Jumping straight to \"here's our method\" "
"without showing why the problem matters. The Problem section is what "
"makes the viewer care."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_paper-explainer.md:255
msgid ""
"**Identical pacing throughout.** The hook and key insight need the most "
"visual energy. The method section can be faster. Evidence should land "
"with impact (pause after showing the big number)."
msgstr ""

